<title>USA: N.J. school district sets vote on $2.65 mln bonds.</title>
<headline>N.J. school district sets vote on $2.65 mln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Board of Education officials in Allendale, N.J., Monday night approved a resolution placing a $2.65 million school bond referendum before voters on Dec 12, a board official said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bonds would pay for improvements to technology and physical education facilities at Northern Highlands Regional High School.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
